# Commits & Releases

## Purpose

Keep history machine-readable and releases automated and correct across independently-versioned
packages.

## Why it exists

A Husky `commit-msg` hook runs `commitlint`, and versioning/changelogs are owned by Changesets.
Bypassing either corrupts the changelog or ships an unversioned change.

## Conventional Commits (enforced)

Every commit message MUST follow the spec or the commit is rejected
([commitlint.config.js](mdc:commitlint.config.js) -> `@commitlint/config-conventional`).

```
<type>(<optional scope>): <description>

feat(express): capture x-forwarded-for as client ip
fix(core): guard empty cache payload
docs: update dev setup
chore: bump dev deps
```

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`,
`chore`, `revert`. Use `!` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer for breaking changes. Prefer the
package as scope (`core`, `express`, `nestjs`, `fastify`, `adonis`, `watchers`, `date`, `ui`).

Pass multiline messages via a HEREDOC to keep formatting intact.

## Changesets (required for user-facing changes)

Any change that affects a published `@lensjs/*` package's behavior or public API needs a
changeset:

```bash
pnpm changeset add
```

- Select the affected package(s) and the correct bump: `patch` (fix), `minor` (additive
  feature), `major` (breaking — signature/export/`exports`/contract change).
- Write a clear summary — it becomes the package `CHANGELOG.md` entry.
- Commit the generated `.changeset/*.md` alongside your code.
- The Changesets config ignores non-published targets — `docs`, `ui`, and the `apps/*` examples
  ([.changeset/config.json](mdc:.changeset/config.json)); changes limited to those need no
  changeset.

## Release workflow

Follow [RELEASE_STEPS.md](mdc:RELEASE_STEPS.md): clean tree -> code + `changeset add` ->
`changeset version` (bumps versions, writes CHANGELOGs, creates per-package tags) -> commit ->
`changeset publish`. `changeset version`/publish own the versions, tags, and changelogs.

## Do NOT

- Hand-edit `version` fields or `CHANGELOG.md` — the tooling owns those.
- Skip hooks (`--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign`).
- Force-push to `main`, or run destructive git commands, unless explicitly asked.
- Commit a user-facing `@lensjs/*` change without a changeset.
- Add a changeset for a docs-only, example-app-only, or internal-tooling change.

## AI must never

- Create a commit whose message would fail commitlint.
- Bump a version or edit a CHANGELOG by hand instead of using Changesets.
- Ship a breaking change as anything less than a `major` changeset.
